From: =?UTF-8?q?Matthias=20M=C3=BCnch?= <claude@djbase.de>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:06:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bebbosshd: fix public-key authentication bypass

A public-key auth QUERY (SSH_MSG_USERAUTH_REQUEST with the boolean 0 and
no signature) only asks whether a key would be accepted; the server
answers SSH_MSG_USERAUTH_PK_OK and must then wait for a signed request
that proves possession of the private key. bebbosshd instead returned
true for the query, so the dispatcher set the session to LOGGEDIN - a
client was authenticated merely for naming a key present in
authorized_keys. Public keys are not secret, so this allowed login
without the private key.

The query path now sends PK_OK and returns false (stays in AUTH); the
login is granted only after ge_verify_ed25519() accepts the signature in
the following request, exactly as the password path requires login().

Verified on the V4SA over a LAN: the normal two-step public-key login
(query -> PK_OK -> signed request -> SUCCESS) and a 1 MiB transfer still
work. Affects bebbosshd only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012seUKBRfgcTt43vbc21K3j
---
 src/sshsession.cpp | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/sshsession.cpp b/src/sshsession.cpp
index 9edd14b..c4a9999 100644
--- a/src/sshsession.cpp
+++ b/src/sshsession.cpp
@@ -1349,13 +1349,19 @@ bool SshSession::handleUserAuthRequest(uint8_t *p) {
 								}
 							}
 						} else {
+							// this is only a "would you accept this key?"
+							// query (no signature). Acknowledge the key with
+							// PK_OK, but do NOT grant the login - the client
+							// must still prove possession of the private key
+							// with a signed request (auth != 0 above). A public
+							// key is not a secret, so returning true here let
+							// anyone in who merely names an authorized key.
 							outdata[5] = SSH_MSG_USERAUTH_PK_OK;
 							memcpy(&outdata[6], blob, 70);
 
 							write(outdata + 5, 71);
 							logme(L_FINE, "@%ld sent SSH_MSG_USERAUTH_PK_OK", sockFd);
-							username = strdup((char *)user);
-							return true;
+							return false; // stay in AUTH, wait for the signature
 						}
 					}
 				}
